# SigNoz SRE Copilot - Cursor Rules

## Architecture Principles
1. All telemetry MUST be OpenTelemetry-native
2. All SigNoz interactions MUST go through MCP Server (JSON-RPC over HTTP)
3. All deployments MUST be reproducible via Foundry (casting.yaml + casting.yaml.lock)
4. All agents MUST emit their own traces (meta-observability)
5. All remediation actions MUST have dry-run mode
6. All MCP queries MUST have fallback to cached data

## Code Style
- Python: PEP 8, type hints required, docstrings for all public methods
- YAML: 2-space indent, no tabs
- All functions >10 lines MUST have OTel spans

## Observability Requirements
- Every function >10 lines MUST have a span
- Every external API call MUST have error handling + span status
- Every agent decision MUST be logged with trace correlation

## Safety Rules
- RemediationEngine defaults to DRY_RUN=true
- Only act on namespaces in ALLOWED_NAMESPACES env var
- Never delete persistent data
- Prefer rolling restart over destructive operations
- Always validate before marking incident resolved

## Testing
- All remediation actions MUST have dry-run mode tests
- All MCP queries MUST have timeout and error handling tests
- Integration tests MUST spin up SigNoz via Docker Compose
- Use pytest for all Python tests

## MCP Server Endpoints
- Health: GET /livez
- Tools: POST /mcp (JSON-RPC 2.0)
- Headers: SIGNOZ-API-KEY for authentication

## Foundry Commands
- foundryctl cast -f casting.yaml    # Deploy full stack
- foundryctl forge -f casting.yaml   # Generate files only
- foundryctl gauge -f casting.yaml   # Validate prerequisites
